# UTM bridge (Cursor → Windows VM)

Cursor has no UTM protocol. The guest RPC is [`Scripts/utm-dev-bridge.sh`](Scripts/utm-dev-bridge.sh). Read [`docs/utm-dev-bridge.md`](docs/utm-dev-bridge.md) before inventing SSH.

## Hard rules

- WPF testhost and the GUI exist only on the UTM Windows guest.
- Runtime root is `C:\dev\BusBuddy-3`. `Z:\` (SPICE WebDAV) is bootstrap only. Never `dotnet build` / `dotnet run` / testhost from `Z:\`.
- Allowed commands:

```bash
./Scripts/utm-dev-bridge.sh doctor
./Scripts/utm-dev-bridge.sh status
./Scripts/utm-dev-bridge.sh sync
./Scripts/utm-dev-bridge.sh exec -- <powershell>
./Scripts/utm-dev-bridge.sh test --filter 'FullyQualifiedName~…'
./Scripts/utm-dev-bridge.sh launch
./Scripts/utm-dev-bridge.sh pull-logs
```

- Read `~/.cache/utm-dev-bridge/status.json` (or `status`) before `doctor`.
- Never start `watch` from an agent.
- Never `dotnet run` the WPF project on the Mac.
- Never `utmctl exec` to launch the app (Session 0 / SYSTEM). `utmctl exec` is OpenSSH bootstrap only (`Scripts/Enable-BusBuddyOpenSSH.ps1`).
- Never `ssh … powershell -Command "…"`. `exec` always uses `-EncodedCommand` (UTF-16LE).
- After a guest run: `pull-logs` and cite the files under `artifacts/utm-runtime-logs-*/`.
